  "question": "A $40\\ \\mu$F capacitor is connected to a $200$ V, $50$ Hz ac supply. The rms value of the current in the circuit is, nearly :",
  "diagram": "",
  "diagram_alt": "",
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$1.7$ A",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$2.05$ A",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$2.5$ A",
      "image": ""
    },
    {
      "text": "$25.1$ A",
      "image": ""
    }
  ],
  "answer": "C",
  "numerical_answer": "",
  "tolerance": "",
  "solution": "$$X_C = \\frac{1}{2\\pi fC} = \\frac{1}{2\\pi \\times 50 \\times 40 \\times 10^{-6}} \\approx 79.6\\ \\Omega$$\n\n$$I_{rms} = \\frac{V_{rms}}{X_C} = \\frac{200}{79.6} \\approx 2.5\\ \\text{A}$$",
